    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 57 Chandlers Rest is a four-bedroom, mid-terraced family home, located in the charming harbour town of Cobh, Co. Cork. Enjoying captivating views of the water, this fine property arrives to the market in good condition throughout, ready for its new owners to move in and make their own.\n\nUpon entering the home, you are greeted by a bright and welcoming entrance hall, providing access throughout the ground floor. To the front sits a generous sitting room, while a fourth bedroom — ideal as a guest room or home office — and a convenient guest WC complete this level. Descending to the lower floor, the heart of the home opens up into a superb open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, a wonderfully spacious and sociable setting ideal for family life and entertaining. A utility room and dedicated storage area are also found on this level, with direct access out to the rear garden.\n\nMoving up to the first floor, a landing provides access to three well-proportioned bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with the added benefit of a private ensuite. A main family bathroom and further storage complete the upper accommodation.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from private off-street parking to the front. To the rear, a private garden provides a pleasant outdoor retreat.\n\nCobh is one of Cork Harbour's most beloved and distinctive towns, offering an excellent range of amenities including schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and regular rail and ferry connections, placing Cork city within easy reach.\n\nThis property is an ideal family home in a truly special setting. To fully appreciate what No. 57 Chandlers Rest has to offer, a viewing is a must. Don't delay — arrange your viewing today!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nThis is a bright and spacious entrance hall, giving access to all accommodation on the ground floor features wood flooring.\n\nSitting Room - 3.39m x 5.56m\nA generously proportioned room, featuring an open fireplace and wood flooring, enjoying wonderful views over the rear garden and out to the water beyond.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.86m x 4.07m\nA generously sized reception room positioned to the front of the property, accessed directly from the entrance hall, with wood flooring throughout.\n\nW.C - 0.87m x 1.87m\nA convenient two-piece suite with wood flooring throughout.\n\nKitchen/Dining/Living Room - 8.41m x 5.59m\nA superb open-plan space forming the heart of the home. The kitchen features a variety of built-in floor and eye-level units along with a range of integrated appliances, with the utility room conveniently accessed off this area. The dining and living space flows openly from the kitchen, laid with tiled flooring and benefitting from ample storage. Double doors lead directly out to the rear garden, while wonderful water views can be enjoyed from this level.\n\nUtility Room - 1.57m x 1.36m\nConvenient utility space accessed just off the kitchen with tiled flooring and plumbed for washing machine and dryer.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.43m x 4.07m\nThis is a large double bedroom to the rear of the home. It benefits from built in wardrobes, a private ensuite and water views.\n\nEnsuite - 2.32m x 1.52m\nPart tiled three-piece suite with electric shower fitting.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.82m x 3.27m\nDouble bedroom positioned to the front of the home with wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.78m x 2.60m\nSingle bedroom to the front with wood flooring features built in storage space.\n\nBathroom - 1.89m x 2.04m\nThis large three-piece bath suite benefits from tiled walls and features an electric shower fitting.\n\n"
      },
